# Faster prompt chunks: three opt-in switches, all off by default. Each gives the prompt other bits than without it;
# decode keeps its bits. Measured on four Sparks cabled as a ring (2026-10-21).
#
# TF_GLM_PROMPT_FP8=1: a prompt chunk's 4-bit dense projections of at least TF_GLM_PROMPT_FP8_MIN_ROWS rows (256) run
#   on TensorFold's own e4m3 tensor-core kernel, qmm.prefill_matmul8 (rows rounded to e4m3 with a scale each, the
#   4-bit weights exact); 1.8x the bf16 prefill kernel on one GB10. +7 % prefill on the ring.
# TF_GLM_PROMPT_W8=1: instead, every 4-bit dense projection also keeps an e4m3 copy of its BF16 checkpoint matrix (a
#   scale a row, about 1.7 GiB a rank), and those prompt projections run on cuBLASLt's FP8 matmul (torch._scaled_mm,
#   row-wise scales; fp32 outputs widened from its bf16 result). The same speed as FP8 on the ring today (the chunk
#   waits on its exchanges), closer to the checkpoint than the 4-bit prompt path: 3.6-3.8 % relative error against
#   the BF16 matrices on random inputs. Decode keeps the 4-bit weights.
# TF_GLM_PROMPT_Y16=1: an EXL3 prompt chunk's routed-expert rows are written as bf16 (prompt_down_kernel's store)
#   and the combine reads bf16: half its traffic. +6.7 % prefill on the ring. The extension builds under its own name
#   (tensorfold_glm_exl3_v21), so an image without this patch keeps its kernel cache.
#
# Drafted replies: with W8 on, drafted replies differ from serial ones ("draft": false) on prompts past ~2K tokens
# (four Sparks, 2026-10-23; each path gives the same reply cold and resumed). With W8 off and every other switch of
# 0124-0127 on, they are equal. Likely cause: the 256-row cutoff and cuBLASLt's per-shape kernels give a prompt other
# bits under other chunkings, and drafted and serial requests chunk a prompt differently. FP8 has the same cutoff and
# was not checked; HANDOFF8 needs W8.
#
# All three are in forward.prompt_arith_code (patch 0107), with TF_GLM_PROMPT_FP8_MIN_ROWS while FP8 or W8 is on:
# ranks started with different switches refuse to start, and a kept state is never resumed under other switches than
# made it. Tests (CPU): tests/cpu/test_prompt_arith_identity.py.

